# Corevia {{stack}} auth starter

Run `php corevia serve`, then visit http://127.0.0.1:8081/register.
The server process must use `APP_URL` matching its browser origin. Production requires an HTTPS APP_URL and APP_ENV=production; .env files are not loaded implicitly.

Routes: /login, /register, /dashboard, POST /logout. JSON: GET /auth/session, GET /auth/me, POST /auth/login, /auth/register, /auth/logout. JSON mutations require the session cookie and X-CSRF-Token from /auth/session. The dashboard requires sign-in. AUTH_REGISTRATION=false disables new accounts.

The default store is private single-node JSON in storage/auth. No database or Node is needed to run the bundled pages. For SQL auth, set AUTH_STORE=sql and AUTH_CONNECTION to an existing named SQLite/MySQL/PostgreSQL connection, then run php corevia auth:migrate explicitly before serving. Changing drivers does not import accounts. Preserve private storage across restarts and serve only public/.

To change styling or the React interface, edit frontend/auth and resources/views/auth. Run npm ci, then npm run build from frontend/auth. Compiled assets and dependency license notices are already included for offline startup. Keep these assets in your application source distribution.

Recovery is available at /forgot-password and verification at /verify-email. Development uses a private preview outbox: php corevia auth:outbox lists messages without links; --show=<file> displays one private preview link. No message is sent externally by preview delivery. Tokens are single-use, expire, and reset revokes account sessions. AUTH_REQUIRE_VERIFIED_EMAIL=true gates the dashboard. Production preview delivery is blocked: configure an AccountDelivery implementation through AUTH_DELIVERY, or keep delivery disabled. Recovery links require JavaScript and use URL fragments so bearer tokens stay out of server request URLs.

MFA, OAuth, persistent remember-me, account management and a bundled production mail transport are not included yet. See docs/v3/auth-storage-recovery.md in the framework for configuration, adapter contracts and remaining scope.
